# Title: Potentially Suspicious Child Process Of Regsvr32
# ID: 6f0947a4-1c5e-4e0d-8ac7-53159b8f23ca
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: elhoim, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-05-05
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1218.010
# Description: Detects potentially suspicious child processes of "regsvr32.exe".
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((process.parent.executable:*\\regsvr32.exe AND (process.executable:*\\calc.exe OR process.executable:*\\cscript.exe OR process.executable:*\\explorer.exe OR process.executable:*\\mshta.exe OR process.executable:*\\net.exe OR process.executable:*\\net1.exe OR process.executable:*\\nltest.exe OR process.executable:*\\notepad.exe OR process.executable:*\\powershell.exe OR process.executable:*\\pwsh.exe OR process.executable:*\\reg.exe OR process.executable:*\\schtasks.exe OR process.executable:*\\werfault.exe OR process.executable:*\\wscript.exe)) AND NOT ((process.executable:*\\werfault.exe AND process.command_line:* -u -p *)))
